domain StructuredSemanticAuthoringKernelDesignV1:
  description "Reasoning for ADR0031 D11 implementation-design candidate revision2."
problem P1:
  |
    Fix implementation contracts that make focused structured semantic authoring
    typed, bounded, recoverable and reusable without activating a runtime route.
evidence E1:
  |
    Accepted ADR0031 D1 through D11 assign orchestration to a thin kernel, domain
    meaning to adapters, effects to ports, and require exact contracts, numbers,
    public mapping, fencing and conformance before runtime adoption.
evidence E2:
  |
    Foundation v3 F5 through F15 and character v5 R6 through R19 require
    adapter-owned focused proposals, transactional staging, complete server
    reconciliation, exceptional five-condition Q&A, source-based retry, cumulative
    resource limits, bounded stall and cycle detection, and trusted-state failure.
evidence E3:
  |
    Current code supplies typed V3 character and migration records, a six-request
    whole-candidate migration loop, family queues and fencing. These are reusable
    seams but do not implement the accepted focused-kernel topology.
evidence E4:
  |
    Corrected review of revision one found two substantive conflicts: its cluster-one-
    only skeleton ordering could not meet character R10 before fan-out, and its
    model-writable set_portrait operation conflicted with character R7 stable-ID
    authority. The owner selected REVISE for those two findings only.
premise C1:
  |
    Current public APIs, current-route limits, immutable generations and activation
    behavior must remain unchanged until later implementation and cutover decisions.
premise U1:
  |
    Provider quality, actual token economics, database DDL details, frontend layout,
    and runtime conformance are unverified. The proposed numerical policy and public
    compatibility mapping require owner review.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, C1, U1:
  |
    Use generic TypeScript kernel state with adapter-concrete source, candidate,
    obligation, work, proposal, finding, question, answer and final types. Decode
    unknown only at external boundaries and forbid JSON-string internal round trips
    and unchecked casts.
decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E2, C1:
  |
    Use server-registered Skill descriptors and work-item sessions exposing at most
    one bounded context query and one proposal or review Tool. Keep full schema and
    candidate server-side. Use adapter-owned closed proposal unions instead of
    generic JSON Patch. Bind common envelope cardinalities and text bounds, derive
    small writable character operations directly to CharacterDefinitionV3 member
    schemas, forbid a general cluster-five candidate write and model-writable portrait
    binding, and allow at most eight conflict-free operations inside the session
    cluster and computed semantic closure while the complete proposal stays within
    six KiB.
decision D3 based_on P1, E1, E2, U1:
  |
    Propose semantic_authoring_policy_v1 with one concurrent request, eight LLM
    calls, forty-eight counted steps, 240 seconds per attempt, 60 seconds per call,
    6000 input and 1500 output tokens per call, 32000 cumulative input, 8000
    cumulative output, 500000 micro-USD estimated cost, eight progress observations
    and two strategy changes. Bind pricing and token-estimator identities and preserve
    the existing six-call route until a later cutover.
decision D4 based_on P1, E1, E2, U1:
  |
    Trigger information-gaining recovery after four no-progress steps and fail after
    three further no-progress steps. Detect three equal states in six observations
    and A-B-A-B in four. Allow adapter-declared temporary regressions for three
    observations without resetting resource or unresolved-cluster history.
decision D5 based_on P1, E1, E2, C1, U1:
  |
    Keep public attempt status values unchanged. Project needs-owner-answer as legacy
    failed plus AUTHORING_OWNER_ANSWER_REQUIRED and an additive ownerInteraction.
    Always append the answer and create a new source-reconstructed attempt rather
    than preserving a suspended checkpoint. Keep cancelled and expired as distinct
    control terminal states, and bind command replay to an exact request digest.
decision D6 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, C1:
  |
    Persist common run, request/accounting, question/answer and final-candidate
    metadata while family ports store typed final payloads. Every mutation compares
    owner, fencing token and run version. Process or lease loss fails the claimed run
    with unknown reservations retained; late results cannot mutate candidate state.
decision D7 based_on P1, E1, E2, C1:
  |
    Require black-box kernel conformance for character, battlefield and narration
    adapters, but wire only the character adapter in a later separately authorized
    runtime slice. Insert this reviewed design gate before the existing B6 task.
decision D8 based_on P1, E1, E2, E4, C1:
  |
    Define the character semantic-skeleton phase across cluster one and only the
    server-designated essential ability or limit and key-relationship claim slices
    from clusters two and three. Permit their focused operations before the checkpoint,
    then fan out remaining dependent work only after passage. Keep portrait binding
    outside the model operation union and preserve it from server authority unless a
    separately authorized server operation changes it.
